---
import PageHead from "../components/PageHead.astro";
import RemovalForm from "../components/RemovalForm.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { getPage } from "../lib/site";

const page = getPage("/privacy");
---
<Base title={page.title} description={page.description} path={page.path}>
  <PageHead
    title="Privacy"
    lead="This site collects one thing: the email address you give us to join early access."
  >
    <p class="muted small">Last updated September 24, 2026</p>
  </PageHead>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>What we store</h2>
      <p>When you join early access, we store:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your email address,</li>
        <li>the date and time you joined,</li>
        <li>the page you joined from (for example, <code>/download</code>),</li>
        <li>the version of the consent text shown next to the form.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        That is all. We do not store your IP address, your browser's user agent, or any other
        information about your device.
      </p>

      <h2>What we use it for</h2>
      <p>
        We use your email address only to contact you about KalCode early access and launch. We do
        not sell it, share it for marketing, or add it to anyone else's list.
      </p>

      <h2>Where it is kept</h2>
      <p>
        The list is stored in a Cloudflare D1 database operated for kalcoded.com. We keep your
        address until you remove it or until we close the early-access list, whichever comes first.
      </p>

      <h2>Cloudflare as our infrastructure provider</h2>
      <p>
        kalcoded.com runs on Cloudflare. Like any network provider, Cloudflare processes technical
        request data — such as your IP address — to deliver pages and protect the site from abuse,
        under its own privacy policy. To stop automated abuse, the early-access form counts
        requests per IP address using Cloudflare's rate limiting; that short-lived counter is not
        stored by us. Our own server logs record errors only and never contain email addresses or
        IP addresses.
      </p>

      <h2>No analytics, no cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This site has no analytics, no tracking pixels, no advertising, and no third-party scripts.
        We set no cookies. Cloudflare may set a strictly necessary security cookie if its bot
        protection is triggered for a request.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you choose a light or dark theme, that choice is saved in your browser's local storage
        and never sent to us.
      </p>

      <h2 id="remove">Remove your email</h2>
      <p>
        Enter the address you used and we will delete it from the early-access list. For your
        privacy, the confirmation is the same whether or not the address was on the list.
      </p>
      <RemovalForm />

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If what we collect changes — for example, when KalCode accounts arrive at launch — we will
        update this notice before the change takes effect and change the date at the top of the
        page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
